  "id": "COMPOUND:249 - PROTEIN:1417",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that sulfanilamide may interact with DNA gyrase subunit B through a common intermediate, the sodium channel protein type 11 subunit alpha. This protein is a target of multiple compounds, including amidepsine D, fuscaxanthone C, and 1,3-diphenylpropan-1-one, all of which are predicted to have a target relationship with DNA gyrase subunit B. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent pattern of interaction, with sulfanilamide being linked to this intermediate, which in turn is linked to DNA gyrase subunit B. The overlapping targets suggest that sulfanilamide may exert its effects through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of the sodium channel protein type 11 subunit alpha, which is a critical component in the regulation of DNA replication and repair. The evidence supports a potential role for sulfanilamide in targeting DNA gyrase subunit B, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
